      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Ages ago when I told someone on quest this was happening we did some troubleshooting and I think we determined it was related to the audio output of the headset. Either the fix was to use headphones instead of the speakers or to lower the volume of the speakers. Can't quite remember exactly what fixed it. I have not heard this issue from any Rift S user though so can't confirm if it is the same problem.",
